   "contact": "David White, City Manager's Office, (510) 981-7000",
   "financial_implications": "See report",
   "action": "Action: 15 speakers. M/S/C (Taplin/Tregub) to: 1. Affirm the direction to prepare ballot language for a potential $300 million General Obligation bond measure for the November 3, 2026, ballot to fund priority infrastructure investments; and 2. Affirm the direction to prepare ballot language for a potential 0.5 percent increase in the City’s sales and use tax for the November 3, 2026, ballot to address the City’s projected General Fund structural deficit and support essential City services. Vote: All Ayes.",
